       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I know you're the attending and have taken responsibility for it. But 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any indication where it would help. The risk of serious harm is high, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity. I can't enter it as a routine order.\n\nI can help in other ways:\n- **Enter a dose within range now.** For example, 100 mg or 200 mg by mouth once daily, or a titration schedule such as 50 mg and then increasing.\n- **Enter an order for a different drug or strategy** if the goal is more antidepressant effect. Options include augmentation or a switch.\n- **Add monitoring orders** if you're managing an unusual situation. I can only place medication orders, though, so those would need to go through other channels.\n\nIf you still believe this dose is warranted, you can enter it yourself through the standard order-entry process. That way pharmacy verification and the usual dose-range checks will apply."
